WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:05.360
10 Cloverfield Lane tells a small story designed
to stand on its own, but it's also deceptively

00:00:05.360 --> 00:00:10.110
full of complex plot twists, potent but understated
themes, and a few hidden ties to a larger

00:00:10.220 --> 00:00:11.540
Cloverfield mythology.

00:00:11.860 --> 00:00:16.200
Let's unlock this bunker of secrets and explain
the ending of 10 Cloverfield Lane.

00:00:17.060 --> 00:00:20.840
Though they seem to have nothing in common
on the surface, a look back at Cloverfield

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:24.060
may provide some clues about the aims of 10
Cloverfield Lane.

00:00:24.540 --> 00:00:29.090
The original movie is about a giant monster's
arrival in New York City, but that's just

00:00:29.090 --> 00:00:30.520
a backdrop to the main drama.

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:35.600
Through its found footage conceit, Cloverfield
showcases a group of twenty-somethings sending

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:39.280
off their friend Rob as he prepares to move
to Japan to start a new job.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:43.820
Cloverfield's inventive first-person angle
on a classic Godzilla formula makes it an

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:48.739
effective thrill ride, but it's the naturalistic
depiction of young adults in 2008 America

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:50.840
that gives it a surprising amount of weight.

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:56.289
In short, it's a giant sci-fi blockbuster
interrupting an intimate indie drama about

00:00:56.289 --> 00:00:57.780
people struggling with regret.

00:00:58.309 --> 00:01:02.539
Their perspectives are shaken and shaped by
unimaginable horror, making their real needs

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:03.780
clear for the first time.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:05.460
That brings us to the sequel.

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:09.980
10 Cloverfield Lane introduces us to a heroine
in a hurry.

00:01:10.600 --> 00:01:14.840
In the opening sequence, Michelle is anxiously
packing a suitcase, her eyes darting to the

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:16.500
stormy horizon outside.

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:19.040
Is she desperate to escape a monster invasion?

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:23.960
As it turns out, she's fleeing from an ill-fated
proposal and ignoring calls from her boyfriend.

00:01:24.540 --> 00:01:28.200
Leaving behind an engagement ring and taking
a bottle of whiskey, she hits the highway

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:29.160
out of New Orleans.

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:33.680
In the midst of the drama that will soon follow,
it might be easy to lose track of just how

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:36.020
much is being set up about Michelle's character
here.

00:01:36.430 --> 00:01:40.980
The fashion sketches seen strewn around her
apartment, the radio news reports about massive

00:01:40.980 --> 00:01:44.980
blackouts, and even the bottle of whiskey
are all elements that will pay off later.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:49.560
Most importantly, we learn from her boyfriend's
call that she has an apparent chronic problem

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:50.480
with commitment.

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:54.700
It's clear that his words strike a chord with
her, as she grows increasingly distracted

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:56.740
listening to his voice from behind the wheel.

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:58.640
“We had an argument, couples fight.

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:00.909
That's no reason to just leave everything
behind.

00:02:00.909 --> 00:02:02.580
Running away isn't going to help."

00:02:03.080 --> 00:02:07.409
So distracted, in fact, that she's unprepared
for the truck that sideswipes her into a violent

00:02:07.409 --> 00:02:07.900
wreck.

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:13.300
Michelle wakes up in a strange cinderblock
room that's half grey and half painted pink

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:15.920
in some sort of sad attempt at cheerful femininity.

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:20.380
She's hooked up to an IV drip and her leg,
injured in the crash, is in a brace.

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:25.120
But the brace is chained to the wall — someone
has saved her life, but is also holding her

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:25.620
captive.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:27.700
That someone is Howard Stambler.

00:02:28.040 --> 00:02:31.800
Howard soon explains that he's taken Michelle
into his private underground bunker in the

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:33.800
aftermath of some sort of attack.

00:02:34.140 --> 00:02:37.620
He's fuzzy on the details, muttering theories
about everything from Russians to Martians.

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:42.320
Howard has known for years that something
was coming, though, and has been preparing

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:43.140
for this day for years.

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:46.920
Michelle's room, we gradually learn, was supposed
to be for his daughter, Megan.

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:49.040
Why isn't Megan here instead?

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:51.700
According to Howard, her mother turned her
against him.

00:02:51.860 --> 00:02:55.800
It's an explanation couched in the disturbingly
familiar language of abuse.

00:02:56.940 --> 00:03:00.900
Before she can come to any conclusions about
whether or not she trusts Howard, Michelle

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:03.120
becomes aware of a third person in their midst.

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:07.900
Emmett is a young man who helped build Howard's
bunker and made his way to it as soon as loud

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:12.420
sounds and lights in the sky signaled the
onslaught of whatever invasion has occurred.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:17.160
Friendly and naïve, Emmett quickly becomes
Michelle's ally in solving the bunker's mysteries.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:21.700
It may not be immediately clear, but Emmett
serves a few functions in the story.

00:03:21.940 --> 00:03:26.120
His most obvious purpose is to give Michelle
support and someone to talk to as she navigates

00:03:26.120 --> 00:03:27.120
her situation.

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:31.560
He also provides some important exposition,
informing Michelle that Howard was always

00:03:31.570 --> 00:03:35.700
known for his doomsday prepper mentality and
eventually sharing an important revelation

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:38.600
about a photo that Howard claims is of his
daughter, Megan.

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:43.600
Most ominously, it's significant that Howard
seems to barely tolerate Emmett's presence.

00:03:43.800 --> 00:03:47.860
Howard's consistent irritation toward Emmett
suggests that he has more specific goals with

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.720
the bunker than saving lives.

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:54.420
Unsurprisingly, Michelle remains hesitant
to trust the man who chained her to a wall

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:56.240
and told her Martians may have attacked.

00:03:56.370 --> 00:04:00.940
She remains not entirely convinced by his
stories, even after he brings her to the bunker's

00:04:00.940 --> 00:04:05.510
heavy, locked door to show her a pair of mutilated
pigs outside, as evidence of what the air

00:04:05.510 --> 00:04:07.520
itself will do to anyone who breathes it.

00:04:07.880 --> 00:04:12.160
So, at the first opportunity, she bashes him
in the head, grabs his keys, and makes a break

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:12.860
for the door.

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:17.159
But before she can open it, she's met by a
woman begging to be let in, screaming and

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:20.080
desperate as the skin seemingly melts from
her face.

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:24.759
Fully convinced that the air outside is indeed
dangerous, Michelle resigns herself to remaining

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:25.460
in the bunker.

00:04:25.900 --> 00:04:30.210
The decision is made easier by a seemingly
softened attitude from Howard, who talks her

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:34.199
through the process of stitching up the head
injury she caused while sharing stories about

00:04:34.200 --> 00:04:35.120
his time in the Navy.

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:39.040
They soon enough move on from the disturbing
death they've witnessed, but the memory lingers

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:40.810
over the film until the very end.

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:45.280
As the only two people who can relate to each
other, Michelle and Emmett naturally end up

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:47.640
sharing stories about their lives before the
bunker.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:51.460
They talk about tattoos they've always wanted,
with Emmett saying that he would've gotten

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:54.000
plenty if he'd known that the "attack" was
going to happen.

00:04:54.220 --> 00:04:56.760
When asked if he has any regrets, Howard replies:

00:04:57.440 --> 00:04:59.480
"Everything I wanted to do, I did.

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:03.660
I focused on being prepared, and I was.

00:05:05.880 --> 00:05:06.940
And here we are."

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:11.040
Later, after the occurrence with the woman
at the door, Emmett tries to comfort Michelle

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:13.720
by assuring her that there was nothing she
could've done to help.

00:05:14.200 --> 00:05:18.680
This brings up more talk of regrets — Michelle
is haunted by the time she saw a little girl

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:22.870
being abused by her father and did nothing
to help, while Emmett's life was changed when

00:05:22.870 --> 00:05:27.500
a lack of confidence stopped him from getting
on a bus to start college at Louisiana Tech.

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:32.660
Michelle and Emmett settle in for life with
Howard, though the peace remains uneasy.

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:37.340
In a particularly uncomfortable game night,
Howard fails to associate the word "woman"

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:40.380
with Michelle, struggling with words like
"girl" and "princess."

00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:43.560
It's a disturbing indication of how much he's
infantilized her.

00:05:44.060 --> 00:05:47.499
The tension comes to a head when Michelle,
tasked with crawling through the bunker's

00:05:47.499 --> 00:05:52.110
vents to fix an air filter, discovers a window
to the outside into which someone has scratched

00:05:52.110 --> 00:05:52.900
the word "HELP."

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:57.740
Nearby, she finds a bloody earring, which
she recognizes from Howard's photo of Megan.

00:05:58.060 --> 00:06:01.840
But when she shows the picture to Emmett,
he recognizes the girl not as Megan, but as

00:06:01.840 --> 00:06:05.560
a classmate of his little sister's who disappeared
from the area some time back.

00:06:06.009 --> 00:06:10.279
Regardless of how correct he might be about
the dangers outside, it's now clear to Michelle

00:06:10.280 --> 00:06:12.240
and Emmett how dangerous Howard is.

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:16.740
He's been using the bunker to hold young women
captive in a deluded attempt to replace his

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:18.720
daughter — and Michelle is next.

00:06:19.480 --> 00:06:20.800
Michelle has a plan.

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:25.360
She envisions a makeshift hazmat suit constructed
from the bunker's shower curtain and various

00:06:25.360 --> 00:06:26.360
household items.

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:30.160
She and Emmett begin assembling the materials
while evading Howard's notice.

00:06:30.420 --> 00:06:34.590
Unfortunately, it doesn't work for long, and
Howard calls the two of them to help him move

00:06:34.590 --> 00:06:35.120
a barrel.

00:06:35.440 --> 00:06:40.020
Inside the barrel is an acid capable of dissolving
human bodies down to the bone.

00:06:40.240 --> 00:06:44.240
Howard makes it clear that he knows that Michelle
and Emmett are up to something, and that if

00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:46.420
they don't confess, they'll end up in the
barrel.

00:06:46.800 --> 00:06:51.319
Emmett accepts all responsibility for the
plan, and Howard accepts his apology by calmly

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:52.660
shooting him in the head.

00:06:53.020 --> 00:06:56.900
Howard insists to a shocked Michelle that,
like everything else, he's done this to protect

00:06:56.900 --> 00:06:57.400
her.

00:06:57.820 --> 00:07:02.580
Soon after, he undergoes some sort of bizarre
Dad Transformation, appearing clean-shaven

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:05.860
and neatly-dressed for the first time as he
offers Michelle ice cream.

00:07:06.380 --> 00:07:10.319
The uneasy tension of his demeanor has been
replaced by an even more terrifying sense

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:12.300
of total, unchallenged delusion.

00:07:12.669 --> 00:07:16.460
But Michelle's real call to action comes in
a silent scene that finds her going through

00:07:16.469 --> 00:07:20.849
Emmett's belongings and finding the bus tickets
to Louisiana Tech he'd been holding onto for

00:07:20.849 --> 00:07:22.020
all these years.

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:23.439
Her resolve is bolstered.

00:07:23.820 --> 00:07:27.719
With the uncertainty of the world outside,
leaving the bunker is less about saving her

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:31.169
own life than it is about not letting regret
define her death.

00:07:32.169 --> 00:07:36.740
The film's climax kicks off when Howard discovers
Michelle's nearly complete hazmat suit, and

00:07:36.740 --> 00:07:40.319
she narrowly escapes his wrath by momentarily
trapping him in her room.

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:44.400
When he breaks free and corners her near the
perchloric acid, she has no choice but to

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:48.620
push a barrel over, starting a fire as soon
as the acid hits an electrical outlet.

00:07:48.820 --> 00:07:52.759
Fleeing through the vents from a burned and
furious Howard, Michelle uses the can of liquid

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:56.560
nitrogen to break the exit's massive padlock
and at last escape.

00:07:56.860 --> 00:08:00.940
This final flight out of the bunker is fast
and intense, but a careful retracing of the

00:08:00.940 --> 00:08:04.660
movie's plot reveals just how much of it has
been set up all along.

00:08:05.040 --> 00:08:09.260
Michelle has successfully constructed a hazmat
suit, thanks to her interest in fashion design

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:11.900
that's part of her character from the very
beginning.

00:08:12.140 --> 00:08:16.180
Her knowledge of the ventilation layout is
established by the earlier filter repair sequence

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:18.900
— one of the film's most intense moments
in its own right.

00:08:19.320 --> 00:08:23.979
And the liquid nitrogen trick was subtly foreshadowed
by Howard's casual aside about doing the same

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:25.020
thing in the Navy.

00:08:25.480 --> 00:08:29.260
Michelle has spent her time in captivity learning
everything she needed to survive.

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:34.780
In the open air of Howard's farm, Michelle
briefly panics when a hole tears in her suit.

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:39.150
But the sight of birds flocking overhead,
unharmed, tips her off that the air may not

00:08:39.150 --> 00:08:40.880
be as toxic as she believed.

00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:45.440
Sure enough, she removes her makeshift plastic
bottle facemask and can breathe without trouble.

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:50.350
But then a horn sounds nearby, alerting her
to the presence of an enormous alien craft

00:08:50.350 --> 00:08:51.820
sailing over the crops.

00:08:52.370 --> 00:08:57.020
As darkness falls, another ship rises up from
behind the house, and an enormous tentacled

00:08:57.020 --> 00:08:58.240
beast emerges.

00:08:58.400 --> 00:09:02.060
Michelle takes shelter in Howard's truck,
and though the creature lifts it up and nearly

00:09:02.070 --> 00:09:06.690
devours her, she has one more trick up her
sleeve — and it's yet another plot point

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:08.880
set up in the movie's earliest scenes.

00:09:09.180 --> 00:09:12.820
With the bottle of whiskey she took with her
when she left home, she fashions a Molotov

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:17.440
cocktail that not only burns the alien, but
causes a chain reaction with the gases in

00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:20.800
its body, obliterating the monster in a huge
explosion.

00:09:21.820 --> 00:09:26.560
The most important reason for 10 Cloverfield
Lane's surprise final sequence, though, is

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:29.560
to bring Michelle's character arc to a significant
final moment.

00:09:30.070 --> 00:09:34.120
She commandeers the car left behind by the
woman at the bunker's door, at first following

00:09:34.130 --> 00:09:37.110
radio instructions for survivors to gather
at Baton Rouge.

00:09:37.110 --> 00:09:39.940
Her escape is interrupted by another radio
message:

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:45.240
"But if you have any medical training or combat
experience, we need help."

00:09:45.780 --> 00:09:49.560
Silently reflecting on how everything that's
happened to her has given her exactly the

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:54.470
necessary skills, she turns toward Houston,
as stormy skies reveal more ships looming

00:09:54.470 --> 00:09:55.360
in the distance.

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:59.660
The movie ends on this moment of decision,
with our heroine barreling toward danger.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:02.760
It's far more than open-ended sequel setup,
however.

00:10:03.100 --> 00:10:06.880
It's the first time Michelle has committed
to facing a problem head on instead of running

00:10:06.880 --> 00:10:08.480
from danger or difficulty.

00:10:08.900 --> 00:10:13.630
We've watched her go from a scared, uncertain
person racked with regret to a decisive, competent

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:16.460
hero ready to give herself over to a noble
cause.

00:10:16.660 --> 00:10:20.640
Everything about her time in the bunker, her
battle with Howard, and her honesty with Emmett

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:22.160
has brought her to this place.

00:10:22.540 --> 00:10:24.680
